(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["test13_1A"] = [{"id":"5179fd36","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Urban planning expert Francisco Lara-Valencia and colleagues have argued that managing environmental matters along the US-Mexico border ______ coordination between the two countries’ governments. Since ecosystems extend across the border, actions taken on one side can have environmental effects on the other side, making international cooperation essential.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Urban planning expert Francisco Lara-Valencia and colleagues have argued that managing environmental matters along the US-Mexico border","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______ coordination between the two countries’ governments. Since ecosystems extend across the border, actions taken on one side can have","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"environmental effects on the other side, making international cooperation essential.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["requires","praises","reports","advises"]},{"id":"a06c434d","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"The work of Kiowa painter T.C. Cannon derives its power in part from the tension among his ______ influences: classic European portraiture, with its realistic treatment of faces; the American pop art movement, with its vivid colors; and flatstyle, the intertribal painting style that rejects the effect of depth typically achieved through shading and perspective.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The work of Kiowa painter T.C. Cannon derives its power in part from the tension among his ______ influences: classic European portraiture, with","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"its realistic treatment of faces; the American pop art movement, with its vivid colors; and flatstyle, the intertribal painting style that rejects the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"effect of depth typically achieved through shading and perspective.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["complementary","unknown","disparate","interchangeable"]},{"id":"8963273a","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Musician Joni Mitchell, who is also a painter, uses images she creates for her album covers to emphasize ideas expressed in her music. For the cover of her album Turbulent Indigo (1994), Mitchell painted a striking self-portrait that closely resembles Vincent van Gogh’s Self-Portrait with Bandaged Ear (1889). The image calls attention to the album’s title song, in which Mitchell sings about the legacy of the postimpressionist painter. In that song, Mitchell also hints that she feels a strong artistic connection to Van Gogh — an idea that is reinforced by her imagery on the cover.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Musician Joni Mitchell, who is also a painter, uses images she creates for her album covers to emphasize ideas expressed in her music. For the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cover of her album Turbulent Indigo (1994), Mitchell painted a striking self-portrait that closely resembles Vincent van Gogh’s Self-Portrait with","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Bandaged Ear (1889). The image calls attention to the album’s title song, in which Mitchell sings about the legacy of the postimpressionist","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"painter. In that song, Mitchell also hints that she feels a strong artistic connection to Van Gogh—an idea that is reinforced by her imagery on the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"cover.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It presents a claim about Mitchell, then gives an example supporting that claim.","It discusses Van Gogh’s influence on Mitchell, then considers Mitchell’s influence on other artists.","It describes a similarity between two artists, then notes a difference between them.","It describes the songs on Turbulent Indigo, then explains how they relate to the album’s cover."]},{"id":"03f5a9b7","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"When marine biologist Brittany Williams played different ocean recordings to groups of oyster larvae, groups that heard sounds of a healthy oyster reef were the most ______. They were twice as likely as other groups to show signs of making a permanent home. This suggests that playing recordings of a healthy ocean reef may encourage oysters to create such a reef.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"When marine biologist Brittany Williams played different ocean recordings to groups of oyster larvae, groups that heard sounds of a healthy","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"oyster reef were the most ______. They were twice as likely as other groups to show signs of making a permanent home. This suggests that","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"playing recordings of a healthy ocean reef may encourage oysters to create such a reef.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["responsive","inactive","liked","distressed"]},{"id":"3654202f","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"Radar and sonar can detect objects or people through walls, but they are too costly for consumer use. Researchers Fadel Adib and Dina Katabi have shown, however, that there may be a comparatively ______ alternative: small changes to the Wi-Fi technology used in smartphones can give users a cheap way to count people or even identify their gestures through walls.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Radar and sonar can detect objects or people through walls, but they are too costly for consumer use. Researchers Fadel Adib and Dina Katabi","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"have shown, however, that there may be a comparatively ______ alternative: small changes to the Wi-Fi technology used in smartphones can give","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"users a cheap way to count people or even identify their gestures through walls.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["infrequent","inexpensive","unmistakable","impractical"]},{"id":"5f56fdec","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from George Marion McClellan’s 1895 poem Eternity. My spirit swoons, and all my senses cry For Ocean’s breast and covering of the sky. Rock me to sleep, ye waves, and outward bound, Just let me drift far out from toil and care, Where lapping of the waves shall be the sound, Which mingled with the winds that gently bear Me on between a peaceful sea and sky, To make my soothing slumberous lullaby.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from George Marion McClellan’s 1895 poem “Eternity.”","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"My spirit swoons, and all my senses cry","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"For Ocean’s breast and covering of the sky.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Rock me to sleep, ye waves, and outward bound,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Just let me drift far out from toil and care,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Where lapping of the waves shall be the sound,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Which mingled with the winds that gently bear","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Me on between a peaceful sea and sky,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"To make my soothing slumberous lullaby.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To illustrate the increasing intensity of the speaker’s desire to escape ongoing hardship by gliding on the ocean","To contrast the demands of the speaker’s everyday life with the serenity of being rocked to sleep by the ocean","To convey the speaker’s longing for the ocean to impart a sense of inner tranquility","To justify the speaker’s qualms about being transported by the ocean to a quiet destination"]},{"id":"b35e2fdc","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Words in Context","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Words in Context","passage":"A casual description of Scherezade García s 2019 mural Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee can make the work seem ______ —a painting that is housed in a coffee shop and that depicts three women drinking coffee may not sound particularly ambitious —but in fact the work is a complex, dynamic meditation on gender and the legacy of colonialism that demands serious attention.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A casual description of Scherezade García’s 2019 mural Blame It on the Bean: The Power of Coffee can make the work seem ______—a painting","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that is housed in a coffee shop and that depicts three women drinking coffee may not sound particularly ambitious—but in fact the work is a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"complex, dynamic meditation on gender and the legacy of colonialism that demands serious attention.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?","choices":["unassuming","shrewd","incongruous","pretentious"]},{"id":"03eeecf3","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from H.D. s 1916 poem Mid-Day. In the poem, the speaker is on a path in an outdoor setting. A slight wind shakes the seed-pods — my thoughts are spent as the black seeds. My thoughts tear me, I dread their fever. I am scattered in its whirl. I am scattered like the hot shrivelled seeds.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from H.D.’s 1916 poem “Mid-Day.” In the poem, the speaker is on a path in an outdoor setting.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"A slight wind shakes the seed-pods—","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"my thoughts are spent","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"as the black seeds.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"My thoughts tear me,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I dread their fever.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I am scattered in its whirl.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I am scattered like","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"the hot shrivelled seeds.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It illustrates a change in the natural environment that the speaker implies is responsible for the growing misgivings described in the text.","It establishes an example of consistency in the natural landscape that the speaker then contrasts with the unpredictability of human emotions.","It presents an observation of an occurrence in the natural world that the speaker then expands on to convey a sense of a turbulent interior state.","It evokes the ordinariness of an event in nature to suggest that the critical self-evaluation the speaker engages in is a common pursuit."],"underline":"A slight wind shakes the seed-pods","underline_segments":["A slight wind shakes the seed-pods"]},{"id":"25176ff8","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"“Mrs. Spring Fragrance” is a 1912 short story by Sui Sin Far. In the story, Mrs. Spring Fragrance, a Chinese immigrant living in Seattle, is traveling in California. In letters to her husband and friend, she demonstrates her concern for what’s happening at her home in Seattle while she is away: ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“Mrs. Spring Fragrance” is a 1912 short story by Sui Sin Far. In the story, Mrs. Spring Fragrance, a Chinese immigrant living in Seattle, is traveling","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"in California. In letters to her husband and friend, she demonstrates her concern for what’s happening at her home in Seattle while she is away:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"______","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from Mrs. Spring Fragrance’s letters most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["“My honorable cousin is preparing for the Fifth Moon Festival, and wishes me to compound for the occasion some American fudge, for which ‘ delectable sweet, made by my clumsy hands, you have sometimes shown a slight prejudice.”","“Next week I accompany Ah Oi to the beauteous town of San Jos é. There will we be met by the son of the Illustrious Teacher.”","“Forget not to care for the cat, the birds, and the flowers. Do not eat too quickly nor fan too vigorously now that the weather is warming.”","“I am enjoying a most agreeable visit, and American friends, as also our own, strive benevolently for the accomplishment of my pleasure.”"]},{"id":"7cbb9764","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Accomplished printmaker and sculptor Elizabeth Catlett (1915 – 2012) used her art to explore the Black experience in the United States. In a paper for an art history class, a student claims that Catlett had a particular talent for unifying various artistic traditions and styles in her work. Which quotation from a scholar describing Catlett’s work would best support","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Accomplished printmaker and sculptor Elizabeth Catlett (1915–2012) used her art to explore the Black experience in the United States. In a","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"paper for an art history class, a student claims that Catlett had a particular talent for unifying various artistic traditions and styles in her work.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from a work by an art historian would best support the student’s claim?","choices":["“In Mother and Child, a sculpture of two Black figures, Catlett used an ancient Indigenous sculpting technique and combined the visual aesthetic of modern Mexican muralists with that of German artist Kathe Kollwitz.”","“In her collage New Generation, Catlett overlaid fabric onto the canvas to represent the clothing of a father and his toddler, positioned to evoke classic images of a mother and child.”","“Created in 1968, Catlett’s sculpture Black Unity, a stylized fist sculpted from mahogany and measuring two feet across, remains an important piece and has received renewed and well-deserved attention in recent years.”","“One series of Catlett’s prints, made by the artist using the linoleum cut method, depicts several notable African American women, including Harriet Tubman and Sojourner Truth.”"]},{"id":"b71861fc","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Percentage of Participants Who Mentioned Factors 80 70 60 50 Percent 40 30 20 10 0 Factor convenience costs established behaviors Researcher Judith Hilton and her team interviewed 55 people about which factors would make them switch from using single-use plastic containers to reusable containers. The graph shows three of the factors mentioned in the interviews and the percentage of participants who mentioned them.","passage_lines":[{"type":"chart","note":"[Graph: Percentage of Participants Who Mentioned Factors — not available here]"},{"type":"text","text":"Researcher Judith Hilton and her team interviewed 55 people about which factors would make them switch from using single-use plastic containers to reusable containers. The graph shows three of the factors mentioned in the interviews and the percentage of participants who mentioned them."}],"question":"According to the graph, about what percentage of participants mentioned costs in the interviews?","choices":["10%","95%","25%","50%"],"unusable":"missing graph"},{"id":"a13c1c66","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Many animals, including humans, must sleep, and sleep is known to have a role in everything from healing injuries to encoding information in long-term memory. But some scientists claim that, from an evolutionary standpoint, deep sleep for hours at a time leaves an animal so vulnerable that the known benefits of sleeping seem insufficient to explain why it became so widespread in the animal kingdom. These scientists therefore imply that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Many animals, including humans, must sleep, and sleep is known to have a role in everything from healing injuries to encoding information in","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"long-term memory. But some scientists claim that, from an evolutionary standpoint, deep sleep for hours at a time leaves an animal so","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"vulnerable that the known benefits of sleeping seem insufficient to explain why it became so widespread in the animal kingdom. These scientists","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"therefore imply that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["prolonged deep sleep is likely advantageous in ways that have yet to be discovered.","most traits perform functions that are hard to understand from an evolutionary standpoint.","it is more important to understand how widespread prolonged deep sleep is than to understand its function.","many traits that provide significant benefits for an animal also likely pose risks to that animal."]},{"id":"cae97f58","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Inferences","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Information and Ideas · Inferences","passage":"Mosses can struggle in harsh desert conditions because these plants require enough sunlight for photosynthesis but not so much that they risk drying out. Researchers Jenna Ekwealor and Kirsten M. Fisher found several species of Syntrichia caninervis, a type of desert moss, growing under quartz crystals in California’s Mojave Desert. To evaluate whether these semitransparent rocks benefited the moss, the researchers compared the shoot tissue, a measure of plant growth, of S. caninervis when growing on the soil surface versus when the moss was growing under the quartz rocks. They found that the shoot tissue was 62% longer for moss growing under the quartz as compared to moss on the soil surface, suggesting that ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Mosses can struggle in harsh desert conditions because these plants require enough sunlight for photosynthesis but not so much that they risk","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"drying out. Researchers Jenna Ekwealor and Kirsten M. Fisher found several species of Syntrichia caninervis, a type of desert moss, growing","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"under quartz crystals in California’s Mojave Desert. To evaluate whether these semitransparent rocks benefited the moss, the researchers","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"compared the shoot tissue, a measure of plant growth, of S. caninervis when growing on the soil surface versus when the moss was growing","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"under the quartz rocks. They found that the shoot tissue was 62% longer for moss growing under the quartz as compared to moss on the soil","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"surface, suggesting that ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice most logically completes the text?","choices":["S. caninervis is one of the few types of moss that can survive under semitransparent rocks.","quartz crystals do not transmit the necessary sunlight for photosynthesis in S. caninervis.","S. caninervis growing under quartz crystals experience lower light intensity and are thus able to retain more moisture.","quartz crystals are capable of supporting S. caninervis growth if the crystals are not too thin."]},{"id":"87023f34","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"“Ghosts of the Old Year” is an early 1900s poem by James Weldon Johnson. In the poem,","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"“Ghosts of the Old Year” is an early 1900s poem by James Weldon Johnson. In the poem, the speaker describes experiencing an ongoing cycle","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"of anticipation followed by regretful reflection: ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation from “Ghosts of the Old Year” most effectively illustrates the claim?","choices":["“What does this brazen tongue declare, / That falling on the midnight air / Brings to my heart a sense of care / Akin to fright?”","“The snow has ceased its fluttering flight, / The wind sunk to a whisper light, / An ominous stillness fills the night, / A pause — a hush.”","“It tells of many a squandered day, / Of slighted gems and treasured clay, / Of precious stores not laid away, / Of fields unreaped.”","“And so the years go swiftly by, / Each, coming, brings ambitions high, / And each, departing, leaves a sigh / Linked to the past.”"]},{"id":"1d08c7ee","domain":"Information and Ideas","skill":"Command of Evidence","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Information and Ideas · Command of Evidence","passage":"Pulitzer Prize – winning writer H éctor Tobar has built a multifaceted career as both a journalist and an author of short stories and novels. In an essay about Tobar’s work, a student claims that Tobar blends his areas of expertise by applying journalism techniques to his creation of works of fiction. Which quotation from a literary critic best supports","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Pulitzer Prize–winning writer Héctor Tobar has built a multifaceted career as both a journalist and an author of short stories and novels. In an","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"essay about Tobar’s work, a student claims that Tobar blends his areas of expertise by applying journalism techniques to his creation of works of","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"fiction.","indent":0}],"question":"Which quotation would best support the student’s claim?","choices":["“For one novel, an imagined account of a real person’s global travels, Tobar approached his subject like a reporter, interviewing people the man had met along the way and researching the man’s own writings.”","“Tobar got his start as a volunteer for El Tecolote, a community newspaper in San Francisco, and wrote for newspapers for years before earning a degree in creative writing and starting to publish works of fiction.”","“Many of Tobar’s notable nonfiction articles are marked by the writer’s use of techniques usually associated with fiction, such as complex narrative structures and the incorporation of symbolism.”","“The protagonist of Tobar’s third novel is a man who wants to be a novelist and keeps notes about interesting people he encounters so he can use them when developing characters for his stories.”"]},{"id":"1d971f75","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Photographer Ansel Adams’s landscape portraits are iconic pieces of American art. However, many of the ______ of landscapes were intended not as art but as marketing; a concessions company at Yosemite National Park had hired Adams to take pictures of the park for restaurant menus and brochures.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Photographer Ansel Adams’s landscape portraits are iconic pieces of American art. However, many of the ______ of landscapes were intended","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"not as art but as marketing; a concessions company at Yosemite National Park had hired Adams to take pictures of the park for restaurant","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"menus and brochures.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["photographer’s early photo’s","photographers early photo’s","photographer’s early photos","photographers early photos"]},{"id":"9df6da04","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Entomologists Yash Sondhi and Samuel Fabian have tried to explain why moths fly erratically around light sources at night. Knowing that flying insects keep their backs pointed toward sunlight during the day, ______","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Entomologists Yash Sondhi and Samuel Fabian have tried to explain why moths fly erratically around light sources at night. Knowing that flying","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"insects keep their backs pointed toward sunlight during the day, ______","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["the researchers theorize that moths, mistaking nighttime lights for the Sun, continually try to reorient their bodies while flying near such lights.","the researchers’ theory is that moths mistake nighttime lights for the Sun, continually trying to reorient their bodies while flying near such lights.","moths mistake nighttime lights for the Sun and continually try to reorient their bodies while flying near such lights, the researchers theorize.","moths continually try to reorient their bodies while flying near nighttime lights, the researchers theorize, mistaking such lights for the Sun."]},{"id":"588887b9","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In 1881, French chemist Camille Faure redesigned the rechargeable lead-acid battery. Faure’s design greatly increased the amount of electricity that the original battery, which the French physicist Gaston Plant é ______ fifteen years earlier, could hold.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"In 1881, French chemist Camille Faure redesigned the rechargeable lead-acid battery. Faure’s design greatly increased the amount of electricity","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that the original battery, which the French physicist Gaston Planté ______ fifteen years earlier, could hold.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["is inventing","will invent","invents","had invented"]},{"id":"59e41600","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"Why are Rome’s famous concrete structures, such as the Colosseum, still standing after 2,000-plus years, when modern concrete may not even last for fifty? Scientists ______ that the secret to Roman concrete’s durability was its unique blend of ingredients, which included volcanic ash and seawater.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Why are Rome’s famous concrete structures, such as the Colosseum, still standing after 2,000-plus years, when modern concrete may not even","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"last for fifty? Scientists ______ that the secret to Roman concrete’s durability was its unique blend of ingredients, which included volcanic ash and","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"seawater.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["explain","having explained","explaining","to explain"]},{"id":"856b495d","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"In the early twentieth century, Joseph Kekuku and other Hawaiian ______ in the mainland United States to the bright and lilting sound of the kīkā kila, or Hawaiian steel guitar. The instrument soon became a fixture in American blues and country music.","question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["musicians introduced audiences","musicians’ introduced audiences’","musician’s introduced audience’s","musicians’ introduced audiences"]},{"id":"a94b7fd6","domain":"Standard English","skill":"Form, Structure, and Sense","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Standard English · Form, Structure, and Sense","passage":"With residents from Mexico, China, El Salvador, and many other countries, Los Angeles has long been a city of cultural diversity. Even back in the 1860s, nearly 30% of the city’s population ______ from outside the United States.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"With residents from Mexico, China, El Salvador, and many other countries, Los Angeles has long been a city of cultural diversity. Even back in the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"1860s, nearly 30% of the city’s population ______ from outside the United States.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?","choices":["is being","was","is","will be"]},{"id":"cfade68d","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Marcela Guerrero is a curator at the Whitney Museum of American Art in New York. She curated the Whitney’s 2018 exhibition Pacha, Llaqta, Wasichay: Indigenous Space, Modern Architecture, New Art. This exhibition featured works by seven emerging Latino artists. She curated the Whitney’s 2020 exhibition Vida Americana: Mexican Muralists Remake American Art, 1925 – 1945. This exhibition included nearly 200 works by twentieth-century Latino and Mexican artists. The student wants to describe the exhibition that Guerrero curated in 2018.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Marcela Guerrero is a curator at the Whitney Museum of American Art in New York.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She curated the Whitney’s 2018 exhibition Pacha, Llaqta, Wasichay: Indigenous Space, Modern Architecture, New Art.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"This exhibition featured works by seven emerging Latino artists.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"She curated the Whitney’s 2020 exhibition Vida Americana: Mexican Muralists Remake American Art, 1925–1945.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"This exhibition included nearly 200 works by twentieth-century Latino and Mexican artists.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Held at the Whitney Museum of American Art, the exhibition Vida Americana: Mexican Muralists Remake American Art, 1925 – 1945 included nearly 200 works by twentieth-century Mexican and Latino artists.","Pacha, Llaqta, Wasichay: Indigenous Space, Modern Architecture, New Art, an exhibition at the Whitney Museum of American Art, featured works by seven emerging Latino artists.","In both 2018 and 2020, Marcela Guerrero curated exhibitions at the Whitney Museum of American Art in New York.","While one exhibition that Marcela Guerrero curated featured works by emerging artists, another included works by twentieth-century artists."]},{"id":"827afb27","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Most conifers (trees belonging to the phylum Coniferophyta) are evergreen. That is, they keep their green leaves or needles year-round. However, not all conifer species are evergreen. Larch trees, ______ lose their needles every fall.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Most conifers (trees belonging to the phylum Coniferophyta)are evergreen. That is, they keep their green leaves or needles year-round. However,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"not all conifer species are evergreen. Larch trees, ______ lose their needles every fall.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["for instance,","nevertheless,","meanwhile,","in addition,"]},{"id":"efa2be4f","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: The meter of a poem is the rhythmic structure or pattern of accents in its lines. Alliterative meter is structured by a pattern of repeated sounds. Quantitative meter is structured by a pattern of long and short syllables. The Old English poem Widsith uses an alliterative meter. The Sanskrit poem Meghad ūta uses a quantitative meter. The student wants to emphasize a difference between the meters of the two poems.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"The meter of a poem is the rhythmic structure or pattern of accents in its lines.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Alliterative meter is structured by a pattern of repeated sounds.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Quantitative meter is structured by a pattern of long and short syllables.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The Old English poem Widsith uses an alliterative meter.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"The Sanskrit poem Meghadūta uses a quantitative meter.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The poem Widsith is written in Old English, but Meghad ūta is written in Sanskrit.","Alliterative meter is a pattern of repeated sounds, but quantitative meter is a rhythmic structure or pattern of accents.","The Sanskrit poem Meghad ūta uses a quantitative meter, while the meter of the Old English poem Widsith uses a pattern of long and short syllables.","The lines of the poem Meghad ūta use a pattern of long and short syllables, whereas Widsith’s lines use a pattern of repeated sounds."]},{"id":"45eaf7fb","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Rhetorical Synthesis","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Expression of Ideas · Rhetorical Synthesis","passage":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes: Tecozautla is a municipality in the state of Hidalgo, Mexico. Municipalities are governmental regions responsible for providing many public services to their residents. One service they provide is street lighting. Tecozautla covers an area of roughly 535 km². Hidalgo is divided into 84 municipalities. The student wants to emphasize the size of Tecozautla.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Tecozautla is a municipality in the state of Hidalgo, Mexico.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Municipalities are governmental regions responsible for providing many public services to their residents.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"One service they provide is street lighting.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Tecozautla covers an area of roughly 535 km².","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"Hidalgo is divided into 84 municipalities.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The municipality of Tecozautla in Hidalgo, Mexico, covers an area of roughly 535 km².","Providing street lighting is just one example of the public services that municipalities provide.","Tecozautla is one of 84 governmental regions, known as municipalities, across Hidalgo.","Tecozautla — a governmental region in the state of Hidalgo, Mexico — provides many public services to its residents."]},{"id":"c7e85c0a","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"The envelope-shaped paper bags common in the US 150 years ago were impractical for carrying goods. ______ because they were the only paper bags that could be mass-produced, these bags dominated the market. That all changed in the 1870s, when industrial designer Margaret Knight patented a machine to make flat-bottomed, foldable paper bags.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The envelope-shaped paper bags common in the US 150 years ago were impractical for carrying goods. ______ because they were the only paper","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"bags that could be mass-produced, these bags dominated the market. That all changed in the 1870s, when industrial designer Margaret Knight","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"patented a machine to make flat-bottomed, foldable paper bags.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["However,","For instance,","Thus,","In other words,"]},{"id":"6916c8e5","domain":"Expression of Ideas","skill":"Transitions","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Expression of Ideas · Transitions","passage":"Laetitia Ky’s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds of shapes. ______ she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa —including the island of Madagascar!","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Laetitia Ky’s hair is her art. Inspired by hairstyles from various African tribes, the Ivorian artist uses wire and thread to sculpt her hair into all kinds","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of shapes. ______ she once made her hair into the shape of the continent of Africa—including the island of Madagascar!","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?","choices":["Soon,","Elsewhere,","For example,","However,"]}];
